hey guys what's up I'm Alana and welcome  to my channel and yes I did just wake up  which is why I look so tired and I also  don't have any makeup on so glossing  over that so the past week has been a GC  at Game Developers Conference in San  Francisco and I've played like maybe 12  hours of VR over the past week in total  I've probably played around maybe 20  hours or so at this point of different  kinds of VR I'm not really sure but the  ones I played the most of have been HTC  5 the psvr  and the oculus rift so obviously I've  been posting about my impressions on  social media and I thought that I would  just group together some of the most  common questions that people have been  asking me about VR and uh answer them so  the first thing that I wanted to address  is is VR actually good or is it a  gimmick and I think VR is incredible  I think PlayStation Move is a gimmick  and I think that you know the Wii monks  were kind of gimmicky but V ah is  amazing as soon as you put that headset  on you feel like you're in a completely  different environment you forget where  you are in the real world  it's it's so good and I think that you  really have to try it to see what it's  like nobody can explain it to you but  it's amazing second would be which of  the three I think is the best and that's  definitely the HTC vive I think it's the  best in pretty much every way it looks  the best you can walk around a space  because it the tracking works incredibly  well so you have quite a large space you  can walk around the input on the  controls it's pretty seamless and it  also has a camera on the front so if  you're gonna run into a wall or anything  you can see the wall and I know come up  and tell you that you're about to run  into something  I think the PS VI is the most  comfortable and it feels the lightest  Sproul by far the easiest to put on as  well the vibe is a little tough to put  on the oculus is somewhere in between  but the psvr is also the cheapest and I  think as a result it is the most grainy  of the bunch  on that note I don't like glasses but  for people who do it said that the PS VI  is the best one for people who  eyeglasses because it's just incredibly  adjustable  but do I think it's worth four hundred  dollars the price point they announced  it for absolutely yes so that would be  the one that I would've bought and I  wouldn't have bought five on oculus  probably  five is a very luxury product you can  trip over the quads do you need a big  space you need to have an open space in  a clear space and you need a PC to run  it so all up it's also an hundred  dollars so combining all of that stuff I  think vibe is the least convenient one  you basically need someone to watch you  play it so that you don't trip all over  yourself it's the best one but it's the  one that I wouldn't recommend to  consumers at this point the oculus is  somewhere in between it doesn't look as  good as survive the camera doesn't pick  up everything quite as well as the vibes  two cameras do and it's a little bit  cheaper at six articles but it's also  probably more comfortable the PS VI is  the cheapest one doesn't look as good  uses the move controllers which are  easily the worst of all of the villa's  controllers that the move control is  outdated technology I really hope that  they upgrade those sometime soon because  it's just not good enough but at the  same time it's also the one that is the  most accessible you just really need a  Playstation 4 run it and also a camera  but everything else comes in the box I  also got a lot of questions about motion  sickness  I personally I'm very susceptible to  motion sickness I get it on trains on  planes and cause I get it all the time  and I do get it more than most people  seem to with VR I played oculus dk1 and  got terrible motion sickness it was so  so bad that I have to sit down for like  20 minutes and drink water and try not  to throw up none of the retail versions  of any of these VI products that I'm  talking about have done that to me at  all been some moments where I felt a  little queasy and there was one point  where I was playing a game that I had  another appointment immediately  afterwards and I skipped it because I  didn't feel great but I think for the  most part it's the consumer release so  the official products are great if you  played oculus dk1 or DK 2 please don't  assume that the full release of the  oculus will do the same thing to you  because it won't it didn't to me so  oculus has this really good system that  I don't know if the others are doing  where they basically label if the game  is intense or comfortable or moderate  and that's how you know if you are  susceptible to motion sickness you  probably wouldn't want to play an  intense game the comfortable games  definitely didn't give me any motion  sickness at any point I've actually  never gotten it from a live game and  I wonder if that is because you're  moving around space or it doesn't feel  like you're what he is doing something  different to what you're seeing the only  time that it's really a problem for me  is if there's a game that has some kind  of strafing like you find me if I'm  strafing and then I see that the what  I'm seeing is strafing but my body is  not that really messes me up I also have  a friend who gets really bad motion  sickness playing any kind of  first-person game and she didn't at all  with the vibe either so you get motion  sickness really badly I just I just want  to say don't rule it out there's a lot  of stuff that works fine I guess a good  follow up for that is um what does it  feel like playing via for a very long  time it's exhausting I played via on  Monday last week for about five hours  straight and I was so tired and I think  that's because you're just constantly  being reintroduced to new environments  so every time you put a headset back on  you're in a completely new place you  have to look around to orientate  yourself all over again figure out  what's around you what way you're going  to go what you've come from it's it's  like traveling in that way it's just  everything is new and it feels like  you're in a different world so you  really have to adjust to that and doing  that that many times in one day like I  did it a lot that Monday and after that  I was just mentally exhausted the  longest that I played a single game hole  was an hour and that was again where I  was sitting it was tower defense it was  a tower defense game so it was obviously  one of the comfortable ones where I  didn't actually have to move but I could  look around the environment sort of see  how everything was going but it was it  wasn't moving so that didn't make me  motion sick at all and I accidentally  played an hour when I thought at  anything fifteen minutes but prior to  last week I didn't actually expect any  kind of side effects and now I am a  little concerned I was very fatigued I  was dizzy  and it definitely hits this strange  point where the real world feels surreal  now gonna go into that too in depth  because it's something that I haven't  yet grasped but I know that I'm not  alone and that other people who have  played VR feel the same pain where it's  like  nothing really feels real anymore it's  very odd I also never had any ice honest  at all I didn't have any ice tray I  didn't get any headaches so really the  only side effects were slight dizziness  and tiredness so I'm pretty sure that  eins is really all of the common  questions that I get if you have any  more feel free to leave my comments  below and all I'll answer as many as I  can but you know if you haven't already  gathered I love we are really passionate  about it I'm so excited for it to come  out and I kind of had this attitude that  anyone who doesn't like VRI thinks it's  a gimmick probably hasn't tried it you  just have to try it for yourself to  understand how impressive it actually is  please try it and then come back here  we'll talk about how great this is it  for me everyone thank you for watching  sorry I look so awful at a very big week  very tired and I'm going to go play a  bunch of the division I will see you  guys next time bye

